---
// Bare document for the numeric-alias redirect stubs (/reference/event-ids/<n>/
// and /reference/network-ports/<n>/). NOT for anything a reader is meant to stay on.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS. Those stubs used BaseLayout, which meant each one shipped the
// nav, the Quick Access sidebar, the Term of the Day ticker, the footer, the
// hover-card engine and every site-wide script — 150,440 bytes — to display 126
// characters of "this page has moved". There are 188 of them (125 event IDs + 63
// ports), so that was 26.9 MB, about 9.4% of the entire build output, for pages
// no one is supposed to read: they are `noindex` and filtered out of the sitemap
// (see astro.config.mjs), and a visitor who lands on one is redirected away
// immediately.
//
// Using BaseLayout was a deliberate authoring choice, not an oversight — the
// original comment explains it was to avoid a second, differently-shaped <html>
// root inside the route file. Moving that root into its own layout keeps that
// property (the route still just picks a layout) while dropping the chrome.
//
// BEHAVIOUR IS UNCHANGED. Same `noindex`, same instant JS redirect, same
// visible fallback link for a no-JS visitor. The only difference is that the
// 150 KB of chrome around that one sentence is gone — which also makes the
// redirect itself faster for the person who hits it.
//
// Styling is a few inline declarations rather than the site stylesheet: pulling
// in the 86 KB Panda bundle to style a sentence that is on screen for one frame
// would defeat the entire point. It only needs to not look broken in the no-JS
// and slow-redirect cases.
interface Props {
  title: string;
  description: string;
}
const { title, description } = Astro.props;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    {/* These pages exist only to forward an old/ambiguous numeric URL to its
        canonical slug. They must never be indexed in their own right. */}
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" />
    <style>
      body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        padding: 2rem;
        font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: #2b2b2b;
        background: #f5f1f2;
      }
      main {
        max-width: 34rem;
      }
      a {
        color: #6b4f8a;
      }
      ul {
        padding-left: 1.1rem;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        body {
          color: #ece6ea;
          background: #1b1518;
        }
        a {
          color: #c9a9e0;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <slot />
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
